1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
Search.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:08,554
Back in episode two we unboxed an app called search.

3
00:00:08,554 --> 00:00:14,778
A view, a template and a URL, all generated for us, and untouched ever since.

4
00:00:14,778 --> 00:00:17,041
It does work out of the box.

5
00:00:17,041 --> 00:00:20,760
Today we find four ways it does not work well.

6
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:26,522
Search for a word in a post's title, and it is found.

7
00:00:26,522 --> 00:00:28,770
A phrase from the intro.

8
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:29,519
Nothing.

9
00:00:29,519 --> 00:00:31,485
A word from the body.

10
00:00:31,485 --> 00:00:32,234
Nothing.

11
00:00:33,034 --> 00:00:36,533
Because the page class only indexes the title.

12
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:40,412
Every other field has to be named in search fields.

13
00:00:40,412 --> 00:00:46,041
Intro and body as search fields, and the date as a filter field for later.

14
00:00:46,041 --> 00:00:49,996
It is not a schema change, so there is no migration.

15
00:00:50,796 --> 00:00:52,502
Fields added.

16
00:00:52,502 --> 00:00:54,208
Search again.

17
00:00:54,208 --> 00:00:56,046
Still nothing.

18
00:00:56,846 --> 00:01:02,543
The search index holds whatever was written when each page was last saved,

19
00:01:02,543 --> 00:01:06,162
and changing search fields does not rewrite it.

20
00:01:06,162 --> 00:01:08,086
Update index rebuilds it.

21
00:01:08,086 --> 00:01:09,395
Nineteen objects.

22
00:01:09,395 --> 00:01:11,474
And now the intro is found.

23
00:01:11,474 --> 00:01:16,016
From here on, publishing a page reindexes it automatically.

24
00:01:16,816 --> 00:01:18,984
Now try a team member's name.

25
00:01:18,984 --> 00:01:21,899
Priya is right there on the About page.

26
00:01:21,899 --> 00:01:23,469
Search finds nothing.

27
00:01:23,469 --> 00:01:26,609
Same for the testimonial on the home page.

28
00:01:26,609 --> 00:01:30,720
The team block fetches its names when the page renders,

29
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:34,010
and the testimonial block only stores an id.

30
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:38,794
So when the page is indexed, that text simply is not part of it.

31
00:01:39,594 --> 00:01:42,263
Blocks have a method for exactly this.

32
00:01:42,263 --> 00:01:47,812
Get searchable content returns the words that should be indexed for this block.

33
00:01:47,812 --> 00:01:52,519
Return the quote and the author, do the same for the team, reindex,

34
00:01:52,519 --> 00:01:54,977
and now Priya finds the About page.

35
00:01:54,977 --> 00:01:56,452
The honest trade off.

36
00:01:56,452 --> 00:02:01,721
Those words are copied into the page's index entry, so if the team changes,

37
00:02:01,721 --> 00:02:06,708
the About page is stale until someone saves it or you run update index.

38
00:02:07,508 --> 00:02:09,249
And this one matters.

39
00:02:09,249 --> 00:02:13,478
I password protected the pricing post and searched.

40
00:02:13,478 --> 00:02:17,540
The query in the generated view still returns it.

41
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:19,862
Add public, and it does not.

42
00:02:20,662 --> 00:02:25,600
The view that Wagtail generates uses live, and live means published.

43
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,286
It does not mean visible to everyone.

44
00:02:28,286 --> 00:02:34,241
So the title of every private page on your site shows up in search results for any

45
00:02:34,241 --> 00:02:34,822
visitor.

46
00:02:34,822 --> 00:02:35,620
Add public.

47
00:02:35,620 --> 00:02:38,307
And add specific while you are there,

48
00:02:38,307 --> 00:02:42,664
so each result is its real page type and can show its intro.

49
00:02:43,464 --> 00:02:45,390
So the view becomes this.

50
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:50,858
Strip the query, search only public live pages as their specific types,

51
00:02:50,858 --> 00:02:56,250
and paginate with get page, exactly like the journal in episode seven.

52
00:02:57,050 --> 00:03:01,623
The template gets a properly labelled search box, a result count,

53
00:03:01,623 --> 00:03:04,507
each result's page type, title and intro,

54
00:03:04,507 --> 00:03:07,884
and pagination links that carry the query along,

55
00:03:07,884 --> 00:03:10,628
which is the lesson from episode eight.

56
00:03:11,428 --> 00:03:14,981
And here it is, with search in the menu.

57
00:03:14,981 --> 00:03:19,510
Handover finds nine pages, across three page types.

58
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:26,832
And a team member's name, which only lives in a snippet, now finds the About page.

59
00:03:27,632 --> 00:03:30,146
Commit, and tag.

60
00:03:30,946 --> 00:03:34,358
And with that, the site is feature complete.

61
00:03:34,358 --> 00:03:36,995
Next episode starts the final act.

62
00:03:36,995 --> 00:03:42,268
Making the admin pleasant for the client who actually has to use it.

63
00:03:43,068 --> 00:03:48,982
Next episode, the editor experience.

64
00:03:48,982 --> 00:03:52,268
Thanks for watching.
